1141: per-edge GLINK/QRTR transport context in beryllium_wlan.c, no behaviour change for the modem. The transport members of the
global `ipc` (SMEM descriptor/FIFOs, intents, TX queue, remote id, QRTR node, packet counters) move into struct glink_edge; the
modem edge is ge_modem, `ge` is the edge the ipc_* functions work on. host (smem partition 0<->host), doorbell, name (log text)
and rx_cb (the QRTR packet handler) are per edge; for the modem they are 1, GLINK_DOORBELL (12), "modem", ipc_qrtr_rx, so every
SMEM address, doorbell write, GLINK/QRTR byte and log line of the modem is as before. The tail of ms_ipc_setup() (descriptor,
TX FIFO, VERSION) becomes ge_setup(). Mechanical: `ipc.<transport member>` -> `ge-><member>` (134 sites).
One thread must drive the edges (ge is a plain pointer): bergamotawlan and bergamotaslpi stay mutually exclusive.

